//
// Probe: which payload arms a Bund program can actually construct.
//
// RFC-0001's criterion 7 asks for a byte-identical wire format "for every
// payload arm a probe can construct on the oracle", and delegates the set to
// this probe rather than asserting a count — two drafts guessed twenty and
// then nineteen, both wrong, because the question is reachability from Bund
// and not the existence of a Rust constructor.
//
// One value of each constructible arm, rendered with its `dt`.
//
"probe: one value per constructible payload arm" println
42            debug.display_stack drop
1.5           debug.display_stack drop
true          debug.display_stack drop
"s"           debug.display_stack drop
nodata        debug.display_stack drop
list          debug.display_stack drop
dict          debug.display_stack drop
valuemap      debug.display_stack drop
metrics       debug.display_stack drop
lambda        debug.display_stack drop
"null" json   debug.display_stack drop
`x            debug.display_stack drop
1 2 pair      debug.display_stack drop
